516	
517	**Files:**
518	- Create: `test/readingTimeMinutes.test.js`
519	- Modify: `src/textstats.js`
520	
521	`readingTimeMinutes` turns a word count into a whole number of minutes. It is the smallest function in the module and depends only on `wordCount`, so it also serves as the check that the three earlier tasks compose.
522	
523	**Behaviour.**
524	
525	- The result is `Math.ceil(wordCount(text) / wpm)`: any text with at least one word takes at least one minute, 200 words take exactly one, 201 words take two, and the empty text takes zero.
526	- `wpm` defaults to 200 when omitted or passed as `undefined`.
527	- `wpm` must be a positive, finite number; fractions such as `150.5` are allowed. Zero, negatives, `NaN`, the infinities and any non-number (including numeric strings and `null`) throw `RangeError` with a message starting `readingTimeMinutes:`.
